           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" id="question-sleep" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-sleep">
               How much sleep do cats need?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-sleep" aria-labelledby="question-sleep">
             <p>
               Most adult cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, while kittens and senior cats may sleep more. Short
               bursts of activity around dawn and dusk are normal because cats are naturally crepuscular.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" id="question-water" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-water">
               Why does my cat ignore the water bowl?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-water" aria-labelledby="question-water">
             <p>
               Some cats prefer moving water or dislike bowls placed near food or litter. A clean wide bowl,
               fresh water, or a pet fountain can encourage healthier drinking habits.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" id="question-scratch" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-scratch">
               How can I reduce unwanted scratching?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-scratch" aria-labelledby="question-scratch">
             <p>
               Offer sturdy scratching posts near favorite areas, reward use of the posts, and protect furniture
               with safe deterrents. Scratching is normal: it stretches muscles, maintains claws, and marks territory.
             </p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </div>
     </main>

     <script>
       document.querySelectorAll(".example").forEach((section) => {
         const button = section.querySelector(".question");
         const details = section.querySelector(".details");

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
         details.hidden = true;

         button.addEventListener("click", () => {
           const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
           button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
           details.hidden = isExpanded;
         });

         button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
           if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
             button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
             details.hidden = true;
           }
         });
       });
     </script>
   </body>
 </html>

